&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;ldquo;Zazastore&amp;rdquo; was a web challenge in PascalCTF 2026. While being a rather easy challenge, it did
showcase a couple of pitfalls in regards to backend design choices and how language quirks can
cause unforseen vulnerabilities if not properly tested.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A &lt;a href="https://github.com/PascalCTF/PascalCTF-2026/tree/main/web02"&gt;handout&lt;/a&gt; containing the backend
source code was provided, but I prefer to have a look at the application in a black box setting
to see what it&amp;rsquo;s meant to do, before I review the code to see how it is accomplished.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>PascalCTF 2026 - YetAnotherNoteTaker</title><link>https://l1ncctf.github.io/post/pascalctf-pwn-yetanothernotetaker/</link><pubDate>Mon, 02 Mar 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://l1ncctf.github.io/post/pascalctf-pwn-yetanothernotetaker/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="teh-vulnerability" id=teh-vulnerability&gt;
